Run gettext's own test suites but not gnulib's self-tests.

gettext-tools/gnulib-tests hangs in the build chroot right after
test-error.sh, holding the worker until its timeout, although the gettext
tests pass. Those tests exercise the vendored portability layer, not
gettext. gettext is several automake trees deep, so a command-line SUBDIRS
override would break the recursion; dropping gnulib-tests from the one
SUBDIRS line that lists it does the same thing precisely.

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -61,4 +61,5 @@
 check() {
   cd ${pkgname}-${pkgver}
+  sed -i '/^SUBDIRS = /s/ gnulib-tests//' gettext-tools/Makefile
   make check
 }
